<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xml:lang="en"><generator uri="https://jekyllrb.com/" version="4.4.1">Jekyll</generator><link href="https://fu-jianyu.github.io/feed.xml" rel="self" type="application/atom+xml"/><link href="https://fu-jianyu.github.io/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en"/><updated>2026-10-24T20:46:43+09:00</updated><id>https://fu-jianyu.github.io/feed.xml</id><title type="html">Jianyu Fu (付舰于)</title><subtitle>Jianyu Fu (付舰于), Ph.D. student at The University of Tokyo, researches human mobility, urban perception, geospatial data science, and multimodal AI for sustainable cities.</subtitle><entry><title type="html">Paper accepted in Landscape and Urban Planning</title><link href="https://fu-jianyu.github.io/blog/2026/lup-paper-accepted/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Paper accepted in Landscape and Urban Planning"/><published>2026-10-23T12:00:00+09:00</published><updated>2026-10-23T12:00:00+09:00</updated><id>https://fu-jianyu.github.io/blog/2026/lup-paper-accepted</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://fu-jianyu.github.io/blog/2026/lup-paper-accepted/"><![CDATA[<p>Our paper <strong>“Evaluating urban street views through collective emotional perception from multimodal social media cityscape posts: An R-ECoT-based interpretable framework”</strong> was accepted by <strong>Landscape and Urban Planning</strong> on <strong>23 October 2026</strong>.</p> <p><strong>JCR Q1 · Impact Factor 11.5</strong></p> <p>Authors: <strong>Jianyu Fu</strong>, X. Wang, J. Ma, C. Zhao, Y. Ogawa, and Y. Sekimoto. I am the first and corresponding author.</p> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/publication_preview/r-ecot-graphical-abstract-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/publication_preview/r-ecot-graphical-abstract-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/publication_preview/r-ecot-graphical-abstract-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/publication_preview/r-ecot-graphical-abstract.png" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" alt="Graphical abstract of the R-ECoT framework linking multimodal social media, collective emotional appraisal, and street-level evidence" data-zoomable="" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> <figcaption class="caption">Graphical abstract of the accepted paper.</figcaption> </figure> <p>The article is in production and <strong>has not yet been published online</strong>. I will share a fuller research introduction and the publication link once it is online.</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Our R-ECoT paper was accepted on 23 October 2026. JCR Q1 · Impact Factor 11.5. Online publication is forthcoming.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Research visit to The University of Hong Kong</title><link href="https://fu-jianyu.github.io/blog/2026/hku-research-visit/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Research visit to The University of Hong Kong"/><published>2026-10-10T12:00:00+09:00</published><updated>2026-10-10T12:00:00+09:00</updated><id>https://fu-jianyu.github.io/blog/2026/hku-research-visit</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://fu-jianyu.github.io/blog/2026/hku-research-visit/"><![CDATA[<figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/hku-2026/group-photo-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/hku-2026/group-photo-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/hku-2026/group-photo-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/hku-2026/group-photo.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" alt="Group photo at the Department of Geography, The University of Hong Kong" data-zoomable="" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> <figcaption class="caption">At the Department of Geography, The University of Hong Kong.</figcaption> </figure> <p>From <strong>5 August to 10 October 2026</strong>, I visited the <strong>Department of Geography, The University of Hong Kong</strong>, as a <strong>visiting Ph.D. researcher</strong>, hosted by <strong>Prof. Bo Huang</strong>.</p> <p>During the visit, I conducted collaborative research on <strong>urban mobility and human behavior</strong>, focusing on spatial patterns of individual travel-time burdens in Greater Paris. The work combined a sanitized GNSS-based mobility dataset with urban spatial information to examine differences in observed travel experiences.</p> <p>The related manuscript, <em>“When mobility continues at a cost: Individual travel-time burdens in Greater Paris,”</em> is <strong>under review</strong>. I am grateful to Prof. Huang and the team for their support and discussions during the visit.</p> <div class="visit-gallery"> <div> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/hku-2026/campus-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/hku-2026/campus-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/hku-2026/campus-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/hku-2026/campus.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" alt="The University of Hong Kong campus and university sign" data-zoomable="" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> <figcaption class="caption">The University of Hong Kong campus.</figcaption> </figure> </div> <div> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/hku-2026/harbour-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/hku-2026/harbour-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/hku-2026/harbour-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/hku-2026/harbour.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" alt="Hong Kong buildings and Victoria Harbour during the research visit" data-zoomable="" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> <figcaption class="caption">A view of Hong Kong during the visit.</figcaption> </figure> </div> <div class="visit-wide"> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/hku-2026/crest-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/hku-2026/crest-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/hku-2026/crest-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/hku-2026/crest.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded" width="100%" height="auto" alt="The University of Hong Kong crest with the motto Sapientia et Virtus" data-zoomable="" loading="lazy" onerror="this.onerror=null; document.querySelectorAll('.responsive-img-srcset').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });"/> </picture> <figcaption class="caption">The university crest: Sapientia et Virtus.</figcaption> </figure> </div> </div>]]></content><author><name></name></author><summary type="html"><![CDATA[A visiting Ph.D. research stay with Prof. Bo Huang in the Department of Geography, from 5 August to 10 October 2026.]]></summary></entry></feed>